insert into public.tips (id, unit_id, title_en, body_md, status) values
  ('667abe18-109e-562c-b974-4938f7888ca3', 'a9fb512f-6297-573c-8d34-be942749040d', 'Entregamos, entregaste', 'The **plazo** moves: they **postergaron la fecha** — *pushed the date back* — or, worse, **la adelantaron**. Then it''s **horas extra** until **entregamos** — *we handed it in*. And the boss asks: **¿ya lo entregaste?**', 'draft'),
  ('5b512731-476b-5b5f-8876-82ce3e6b19a4', 'a9fb512f-6297-573c-8d34-be942749040d', 'Sobre la hora', '**Sobre la hora** — *right at the deadline, with seconds to spare* — is how most porteño projects get done. First a **borrador** — *a draft* — then you **corregir** it, and only then the **informe** or the **presentación**. **¿Avanzaron?** — *any progress?*', 'draft'),
  ('0f9e71c8-7258-59a6-9ca3-5d3ae23d9539', '112b1b4f-7388-538e-9734-dab36a241ad2', 'Se lo merece, nos lo merecemos', '**Merecerse** keeps its pronoun for every person: **me lo merezco**, **te lo merecés**, **se lo merece** — *she deserves it* — **nos lo merecemos** — *we deserve it*. A **gerente** who sees your **responsabilidad** grow should hear it: **se merece el ascenso**.', 'draft'),
  ('906103c0-8825-51f0-8f33-0bb01926b4d9', '112b1b4f-7388-538e-9734-dab36a241ad2', 'En blanco, en negro', 'Before you **negociar**, know what you''re owed. A job **en blanco** is *on the books*, with aguinaldo and obra social; **en negro** is *off the books*. And with inflation, the yearly **ajuste** — *the pay adjustment* — is the first thing you **exigir**.', 'draft'),
  ('651372f8-ada8-596c-b92d-a40cf7df568f', 'd8bc6075-554e-5b94-9a5b-df5e1686741a', 'Me hace ruido', 'When something doesn''t sit right: **me hace ruido** — *something''s off about it* — and **no me cierra** — *it doesn''t add up*. Porteños say both about a deal, a story, or a new boyfriend.', 'draft'),
  ('0904d601-7430-56cd-9bf0-9e5b17a157e0', 'd8bc6075-554e-5b94-9a5b-df5e1686741a', 'Me quedé helado', 'The same shape as **me cayó la ficha** — the feeling happens *to* you: **me quedé helado** — *I froze, I was stunned*; **me dejó pensando** — *it got me thinking*; **me partió el alma** — *it broke my heart*. The good ones: **me hace bien**, **me da ternura**, and **¡qué alivio!**', 'draft'),
  ('c4d61984-886d-5f1c-85e3-6db107bc6b5a', '512c0d0a-584d-5403-9bcf-d9c74d8ceb43', 'Sobre la hora, se lo merece', '**Entregamos sobre la hora**, **postergaron la fecha**; **se lo merece**, **nos lo merecemos** — work, every person.', 'draft'),
  ('a34223c2-0e77-5292-af66-2d1ef580ba10', '512c0d0a-584d-5403-9bcf-d9c74d8ceb43', 'Me hace ruido', '**Me hace ruido**, **no me cierra**, **me quedé helado**, **qué alivio** — the gut, in porteño.', 'draft'),
  ('22e7eebe-f6ca-564c-96ff-51d87aa19bcf', 'ad17a937-2fe2-519e-9f42-86f123c7e38c', 'Acampamos, recorrieron', 'Travel stories run on the preterite: **acampamos** — *we camped* — **hicimos dedo** — *we hitchhiked* — **¿recorriste el norte?**, **mis viejos recorrieron la costa**. Distances are in **kilómetros**, and in the south there are always more than you thought.', 'draft'),
  ('b4d85210-f57c-504d-a015-0281e2125c5a', 'ad17a937-2fe2-519e-9f42-86f123c7e38c', 'La cordillera', 'The **cordillera** — *the Andes range* — runs down the whole west: **lagos** and **nieve** in the south, **bodegas** — *wineries* — in Mendoza, red **valles** in Jujuy. A **mochilero** does it all with a backpack and a carpa, down to Ushuaia.', 'draft'),
  ('088111ce-f197-57ed-a80c-180b1990da3e', 'da7656d3-0e9b-597b-ac1d-493e481b96f5', 'Calentá el agua, no la hiervas', 'The rules of the one who ceba: **calentá el agua** in the pava — *heat the water* — but **no la hiervas**: water that **hierve** burns the yerba. **Yo cebo**, you drink. When there''s no taste left, **el mate está lavado** — *washed out* — and it''s time to change the yerba.', 'draft'),
  ('a27610da-e63d-5d19-9150-fec8001c9793', 'da7656d3-0e9b-597b-ac1d-493e481b96f5', '¿Te convido?', '**Convidar** is *to offer, to share what''s yours*: **¿te convido un mate?**, **convidame uno**. Afternoon **merienda** means mate with **bizcochitos**, or **tortas fritas** when it rains. A **matero** drinks it all day; kids get **mate cocido**, the tea-bag version.', 'draft'),
  ('4039fa21-f933-5aec-877d-701a109a210b', '0dacd2e3-2a45-5ad7-a13d-42f6b718c484', 'Se instalaron', 'The family story runs in the third person plural: **se escaparon de la guerra**, **se instalaron en un conventillo** — *a crowded tenement house* — and **trabajaron en el puerto**. One person: **se instaló**. They left **pobreza** behind and **conservaron** the recipes.', 'draft'),
  ('69083595-4dc0-5d7d-8816-d2abf4a0f8c7', '0dacd2e3-2a45-5ad7-a13d-42f6b718c484', 'Gallego y la ciudadanía', 'In Argentina every Spaniard is a **gallego**, from Galicia or not. And the great-grandparents still pay off: half of Buenos Aires is sacando **la ciudadanía** italiana or española. Your **raíces** — *roots* — come with a passport.', 'draft'),
  ('9f9ceb73-2afc-50c6-b957-5e19f23e93c9', '7213df53-3f20-5649-8b69-0dacbe10f0d7', 'Acampamos, te convido', '**Acampamos al lado de un lago**, **hicimos dedo**; **¿te convido un mate?** — but **no hiervas el agua**.', 'draft'),
  ('8a066e8b-2707-5c72-983a-941cafd3d280', '7213df53-3f20-5649-8b69-0dacbe10f0d7', 'Se instalaron', '**Se escaparon de la guerra**, **se instalaron en La Boca** — the roots of the city.', 'draft'),
  ('6044efe3-ab79-5a6e-bf86-377632411a37', '08db04c7-6430-585e-8d87-f26f0376c7ad', 'Te estaba tomando el pelo', '**Estar** + the **-ando / -iendo** form is how you catch a joke in progress: **me estás tomando el pelo** — *you''re pulling my leg*; **¿me estás jodiendo?** — *you''re kidding me*; **estás exagerando**. And when you believed it: **¡caíste!** — *got you!* — **qué inocente**.', 'draft'),
  ('a3dfd806-54f5-516a-a10e-12f1e87569d8', '08db04c7-6430-585e-8d87-f26f0376c7ad', 'No te piques', 'The joke only works if you don''t **picarse** — *get touchy*: **se picó** is the worst thing to say about someone at an asado. Everybody has an **apodo** — *a nickname* — and a **broma** — *a prank* — is a sign of affection. **No te hagas el vivo**, though: **te hacés el vivo** is *you''re acting smart*.', 'draft'),
  ('50e380f6-2638-5de1-b5c1-fd6096d6cbca', '06821d8b-7d2f-5276-b374-2844bb3b99d6', 'Se recibió, se jubiló', 'Life''s big steps take the pronoun, like **se casó**: **se recibió** — *graduated* (from the facu, with a title: **se recibió de abogado**) — **me recibí**, **se comprometieron** — *they got engaged* — **se jubiló** — *retired*. The sad one too: **se murió** — *died*.', 'draft'),
  ('fcd34b7a-a72e-5992-8c6c-e82915d7622a', '06821d8b-7d2f-5276-b374-2844bb3b99d6', 'Por civil, y el velorio', 'Porteños get married **por civil** — *at the registry office* — often with a **padrino** and a **madrina**, then the **luna de miel**. When **nació una nena** or **un nene**, you visit. At a **velorio** — *a wake* — you hug and say **te acompaño en el sentimiento**.', 'draft'),
  ('17a11c47-ddcf-52c0-865b-41a1aed9e668', '132415fc-1b04-527c-a000-1361223954c5', 'Se emocionó, nos emocionamos', '**Emocionarse** in every person: **me emocioné**, **¿te emocionaste?**, **mi viejo se emocionó**, **nos emocionamos todos**. It was **emotivo** — *moving* — and **se me hizo un nudo en la garganta** — *I got a lump in my throat*.', 'draft'),
  ('a25e7141-158e-5b98-ad99-7895076ecc1f', '132415fc-1b04-527c-a000-1361223954c5', 'Me llegó', '**Me llegó** — *it really touched me*: **tu mensaje me llegó un montón**. Say it **de todo corazón**. **Sos un orgullo** — *you make us proud*. After the **discurso**, everyone **se abrazó** — and the **felicidad** was all over the room.', 'draft'),
  ('72041628-e505-5055-893b-2971932a487a', '5ebbe531-b8e4-58e6-9eb8-b9340f28458c', '¡Caíste!', '**Te estaba tomando el pelo**, **¡caíste!**, **no te piques** — the wind-up, in porteño.', 'draft'),
  ('d3c1b17e-2938-5068-9e90-ab4c6a0edcec', '5ebbe531-b8e4-58e6-9eb8-b9340f28458c', 'Se recibió, se emocionó', '**Se recibió**, **se comprometieron**, **se jubiló** — and **se emocionó**, **nos emocionamos**, **me llegó**.', 'draft'),
  ('36794004-344e-51d8-96d4-0a9ba3a15337', '6da6ead7-b546-54e5-b84f-a16a56ef3f2a', 'Al principio me costó', 'Looking back is the preterite: **al principio me costó** — *it was hard at first* — **pero me adapté** — *I adapted*. Now **me siento como en casa**. Say it **de corazón**.', 'draft'),
  ('cf2878f8-b900-509f-b7ce-8ab38a91c757', '6da6ead7-b546-54e5-b84f-a16a56ef3f2a', 'Brindemos', 'A porteño **despedida** — *farewell party* — ends with a toast: **¡brindemos!**, **brindo por ustedes**. Then **gracias por todo**, **fue un placer**, and never *adiós*: **me despido** with **hasta la próxima**, because here nobody really leaves.', 'draft')
